statement:
Let $A$ be a finite set (possibly empty), $S$ a scheme [def-pc-scheme] and $g_a:V_a\to S$ ($a\in A$) morphisms of schemes. Let $V=\coprod_{a\in A}V_a$ be the coproduct in the category of schemes, with coprojections $\iota_a:V_a\to V$ [lem-weil-pbc-scheme-coproduct-family], and let $g:V\to S$ be the unique morphism with $g\circ\iota_a=g_a$ for all $a\in A$. Then:
(1) if every scheme $V_a$ is quasi-compact (its underlying space is quasi-compact), then $V$ is quasi-compact; if every $V_a$ is quasi-separated (its morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ is quasi-separated [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions]), then $V$ is quasi-separated;
(2) if every $g_a$ is locally of finite presentation [def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation], then $g$ is locally of finite presentation.
